# WAF quarantine (runner + worker)

Per **(worker node, canonical target)** Redis reputation blocks nodes that hit WAF challenges; heavy HTTP jobs get `NodeAffinity` `NotIn` on **`WAF_NODE_LABEL`** (default `kubernetes.io/hostname`). The **precheck** issues one worker **Job per node**, pinned with **`required_nodes` → affinity `In`=[that host], and pumps all pending targets through one nuclei stdin on that Pod (not one Job per `(target × node)`). Worker Pods expose **`NODE_NAME` / `POD_NAME`** via Downward API; NATS payloads include **`node_name` / `pod_name`** for attribution.

The runner discovers labeled worker nodes with **`KubernetesService.list_worker_nodes`** (Kube API `nodes` **list**, cluster-scoped). The ServiceAccount needs **`reconhawx-runner-node-reader`** (`kubernetes/base/runner/runner-rbac.yaml` — **`ClusterRole` + `ClusterRoleBinding`** bound to **`runner-service-account`**). Fresh installs/upgrades applying `kubernetes/base/` or **`base-update/`** pick this up; if you pasted an older RBAC snippet, re-apply the bundle so precheck does not silently skip (**`WAF_DETECTION=off`** is unrelated).

